window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2795ffa779d8d302"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"follow-a-goal\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">持续推进一个目标</h1> <p>为 Codex 设定一个用于长时间工作的持久目标。</p> <p>当任务需要 Codex 跨多个回合持续工作，朝可验证的停止条件推进时，使用 <code>/goal</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>具有明确成功条件和验证循环的长时间编程工作。</li> <li>Codex 可以在限定范围内持续推进的代码迁移、大型重构、部署重试循环、实验、 游戏和个人项目。</li> <li>需要按明确成功标准开展长时间实验的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>设置长时间目标</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal 完成 [objective]，持续工作，直到达到 [verifiable end state]。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">CLI 斜杠命令中的 <code>/goal</code>（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">Codex 工作流</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-71636f336b61afaa\">执行代码迁移</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4efcc7a3b951adb1\">迭代解决难题</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾加上 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">简介</h2> <p>如果希望 Codex 持续朝一个持久目标推进，而不是在普通的一个回合后停下，可以使用 <code>/goal</code>。它适合有明确目标、验证循环，以及足够推进空间的工作，让 Codex 不必每一步都请你指引。使用 <code>/goal</code> 后，Codex 可以独立工作数小时，而不需要你继续提供输入。</p> <p>用 <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code> 设置目标，用 <code>/goal</code> 检查当前目标；需要控制运行时，可以使用 <code>/goal pause</code>、<code>/goal resume</code> 或 <code>/goal clear</code>。</p> <p>如果斜杠命令列表中没有 <code>/goal</code>，请启用 <code>features.goals</code>，配置位于 <code>config.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\ngoals = true\n</code></pre> <p>你也可以在 CLI 中运行 <code>codex features enable goals</code>，或者让 Codex 运行这个命令。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-right-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">选择合适的工作</h2> <p>一个好的目标应比单条提示词的范围更大，又比没有明确终点的待办清单更小。它应明确 Codex 要实现什么、不能改动什么、如何验证进展，以及何时停止。</p> <p>以下工作适合使用目标：</p> <ul> <li>目标技术栈、行为一致性检查和约束都很明确的代码迁移</li> <li>Codex 可以在每个检查点之后运行测试的大型重构</li> <li>Codex 可以持续改进一个可运行成果的实验、游戏或原型</li> </ul> <p>避免把互不相关、缺乏明确约束的一串工作设为一个目标。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-loop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">建立工作循环</h2> <ol> <li>指定一个目标和一个停止条件。</li> <li>告诉 Codex 必须先读取哪些文件、文档、问题单、日志或计划。</li> <li>明确哪些命令或成果文件能证明进展。</li> <li>要求 Codex 按检查点推进，并保留简短的进度日志。</li> <li>运行过程中，使用 <code>/goal</code> 查看状态。</li> <li>工作完成、受阻或需要改变方向时，可以暂停、恢复或清除目标。</li> </ol> <p>关键在于明确约定。在开始之前，Codex 就应知道什么才算“完成”。如果目标是迁移，“完成”可以指新路径通过契约测试，并且旧路径仍有回滚方案。如果目标是游戏或原型，“完成”可以指应用能构建、启动，并且符合输入参考或预期行为。</p> <p>可以请 Codex 帮忙：先聊聊你想构建什么，再让它直接设置目标并开始工作。</p> <p><a id=\"let-codex-work-independently\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">让 Codex 独立工作</h2> <p>目标运行期间，可以要求简明的进度报告，让过程更容易信任。一份有用的状态更新会说明当前检查点、已验证的内容、剩余工作，以及 Codex 是否受阻。 如果状态变得含糊，应收紧目标，而不是添加更多零散指令。明确告诉 Codex 下一个重要检查点是什么、哪个命令可以证明它已达到，以及什么情况应使它暂停。</p> <p>Codex 持续推进目标时，可以独立工作很多小时，不需要你反复查看。它会在确信已达到停止条件时结束运行，因此你可以把 <code>/goal</code> 看作一项无需一直监看的后台任务。</p> <p><a id=\"example-goals\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">目标示例</h2> <p><a id=\"migrations\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">迁移</h3> <p>无论是将游戏迁移到新的技术栈、将移动应用迁移到新平台，还是将代码库迁移到新框架，都可以使用 <code>/goal</code> 让 Codex 执行迁移：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Migrate this project from [legacy stack or system] to [target stack or system]. Make sure all screens stay exactly the same visually, using playwright interactive to verify the output.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">/goal 将这个项目从 [legacy stack or system] 迁移到 [target stack or system]。确保所有界面的视觉表现完全保持一致，并使用 playwright interactive 验证输出。</div></div> <p><a id=\"prototype-creation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">创建原型</h3> <p>无论是从零创建新应用、新游戏还是新功能，都可以使用 <code>/goal</code> 让 Codex 完成一个完善的首版。你可以用 PLAN.md 文件指导首版制作，准确描述希望构建的内容。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Implement PLAN.md, creating tests for each milestone and verifying the output with playwright interactive. [include reference screens as needed]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">/goal 实施 PLAN.md，为每个里程碑创建测试，并使用 playwright interactive 验证输出。[include reference screens as needed]</div></div> <p><a id=\"prompt-optimization\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">优化提示词</h3> <p>如果你有一套评测，可以使用 <code>/goal</code> 根据评测结果优化提示词。Codex 可以检查失败案例、更新提示词、重新运行评测，并持续迭代，直到分数提高或达到你设定的停止条件。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Optimize the prompts in [prompt file or directory] until the eval suite reaches [target score or pass rate]. After each change, run [eval command], inspect the failing cases, and keep the prompt edits minimal and targeted. Stop when the target is met or when further prompt changes would need product or policy guidance.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">/goal 优化 [prompt file or directory] 中的提示词，直到评测套件达到 [target score or pass rate]。每次更改后，运行 [eval command]，检查失败用例，并让提示词修改保持最小且有针对性。达到目标时停止；如果继续修改提示词需要产品或政策方面的指导，也应停止。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"follow-a-goal\">Follow a goal</h1> <p>Give Codex a durable objective for long-running work.</p> <p>Use <code>/goal</code> when a task needs Codex to keep working across turns toward a verifiable stopping condition.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Long-running coding work with a clear success condition and validation loop.</li> <li>Code migrations, large refactors, deployment retry loops, experiments, games, and side projects where Codex can keep making scoped progress.</li> <li>Teams that need to run long experiments with clear success criteria.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Set a Long-Running Goal</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Complete [objective] without stopping until [verifiable end state].\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\"><code>/goal</code> in CLI slash commands (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Local page (section not recognized)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">Codex workflows</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-71636f336b61afaa\">Run code migrations</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4efcc7a3b951adb1\">Iterate on difficult problems</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Use <code>/goal</code> when you want Codex to keep working toward one durable objective instead of stopping after one normal turn. It's useful for work that has a clear target, a validation loop, and enough room for Codex to make progress without asking you to steer every step. When you use <code>/goal</code>, Codex can work independently for multiple hours without needing your input.</p> <p>Set a goal with <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code>, check the current goal with <code>/goal</code>, and use <code>/goal pause</code>, <code>/goal resume</code>, or <code>/goal clear</code> when you need to control the run.</p> <p>If <code>/goal</code> doesn't appear in the slash command list, enable <code>features.goals</code> in <code>config.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[features]\ngoals = true\n</code></pre> <p>You can also run <code>codex features enable goals</code> from the CLI or ask Codex to run it.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-the-right-work\">Choose the right work</h2> <p>A good goal is bigger than one prompt but smaller than an open-ended backlog. It should define what Codex should achieve, what it shouldn't change, how it should validate progress, and when it should stop.</p> <p>This works well for:</p> <ul> <li>code migration where the target stack, parity checks, and constraints are clear</li> <li>large refactors where Codex can run tests after each checkpoint</li> <li>experiments, games, or prototypes where Codex can keep improving a working artifact</li> </ul> <p>Avoid using a goal for a loose list of unrelated work.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-the-loop\">Set up the loop</h2> <ol> <li>Name one objective and one stopping condition.</li> <li>Point Codex at the files, docs, issue, logs, or plan it must read first.</li> <li>Define the commands or artifacts that prove progress.</li> <li>Tell Codex to work in checkpoints and keep a short progress log.</li> <li>Use <code>/goal</code> to inspect status while it runs.</li> <li>Pause, resume, or clear the goal when the run is done, blocked, or changing direction.</li> </ol> <p>The important part is the contract. Codex should know what \"done\" means before it starts. If the goal is a migration, \"done\" might mean the new path passes contract tests and the legacy path still has a rollback. If the goal is a game or prototype, \"done\" might mean the app builds, launches, and matches the input reference or expected behavior.</p> <p>Ask Codex to help: start by having a conversation about what you want to build, then ask it to directly set a goal and start working.</p> <h2 id=\"let-codex-work-independently\">Let Codex work independently</h2> <p>During a goal, ask for compact progress reports that make the run easier to trust. A useful status update names the current checkpoint, what was verified, what remains, and whether Codex is blocked. If the status becomes vague, tighten the goal rather than adding more one-off instructions. Tell Codex exactly which checkpoint matters next, which command proves it, and what should cause it to pause.</p> <p>When Codex follows a goal, it can work independently for many hours without you having to check in. It will stop running when it's confident it has reached the stopping condition, so you should think of <code>/goal</code> as a background task you don't need to monitor.</p> <h2 id=\"example-goals\">Example goals</h2> <h3 id=\"migrations\">Migrations</h3> <p>Whether you're migrating games to a new stack, mobile apps to a new platform, or a codebase to a new framework, you can use <code>/goal</code> to have Codex run the migration:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Migrate this project from [legacy stack or system] to [target stack or system]. Make sure all screens stay exactly the same visually, using playwright interactive to verify the output.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"prototype-creation\">Prototype creation</h3> <p>Whether you're creating a new app from scratch, a new game, or a new feature, you can use <code>/goal</code> to have Codex complete a polished first version. You can use a PLAN.md file to guide the creation of the first version, describing precisely what you want to build.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Implement PLAN.md, creating tests for each milestone and verifying the output with playwright interactive. [include reference screens as needed]\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"prompt-optimization\">Prompt optimization</h3> <p>When you have an eval suite, you can use <code>/goal</code> to optimize prompts against the eval results. Codex can inspect failures, update the prompt, rerun the evals, and keep iterating until the score improves or it reaches your stopping condition.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">/goal Optimize the prompts in [prompt file or directory] until the eval suite reaches [target score or pass rate]. After each change, run [eval command], inspect the failing cases, and keep the prompt edits minimal and targeted. Stop when the target is met or when further prompt changes would need product or policy guidance.\n</code></pre>"};
